      "content": "It's incredibly compassionate of you to reflect on the impact of your struggles on your partner and family, and it shows how much you care. I hear your concern about being a 'shadow' over them. While this thought is heart-tugging, remember that healing is a process, and your effort to get better is a sign of self-respect and care. The goal isn't for others to live their lives without you; it's to live your life fully again and be present with those who love you. Asking for help is a crucial step in dismantling those burdens. You don't have to do this alone, and with time and support, you can find a balance where you stop being a hindrance and become a full, healthy presence in their lives—and in your own. Would it help to explore some constructive resources now?",
